{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"99d44ab5-dfce-44d7-9375-257db7b6ab85","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The 500 error was caused by storing raw `float` values in DynamoDB (the similarity scores). DynamoDB only accepts `Decimal` objects for numeric attributes, so the second publish failed when the `similar` list contained floats.\n\n**Fix applied**\n1. Imported `Decimal` in `src/app.py`.\n2. Converted each similarity score to `Decimal` before storing:\n```python\nscored.append({\"slug\": other[\"slug\"], \"score\": Decimal(str(similarity(story, other)))})\n```\n\nThese changes prevent the TypeError and allow subsequent publishes to succeed.\n\nYou can review the changes and the full explanation in the generated answer file:\n\n- Updated source: [src/app.py](file:///tmp/h-aGEpbP/src/app.py)\n- Explanation \u0026 fix details: [ANSWER.md](file:///Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/99d44ab5-dfce-44d7-9375-257db7b6ab85/ANSWER.md)\n","duration_seconds":35.962814,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":12162,"output_tokens":3140,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":49920,"total_tokens":15302}}}
